Well.

I've been at this game, in various versions, for about five years now.

V1.0.4 (Mac) -- I won after about a year of playing.
V3.0j  (PC)  -- Took another four years to ascend.
V3.1.3 (PC)  -- Took two weeks.

Firstly, many kudos to the dev. team; 3.1.3 is vastly superior to 3.0j,
both in terms of user interface (just nicer in every way) and, I feel,
game play/balance ("You destroy the minotaur!  But wait... the minotaur's
medallion begins to glow!"  "The wand misses you!"  "The Wizard of Yendor
quaffs a potion of gain level!  The Wizard of Yendor seems more experienced!"
Can we spell "frustration", children?)

Anyway, I ascended.  No polypiling, saved-game copying, Bell abuse or
artifact wishing.  HOWEVER, I wouldn't have done it without the spoilers
I read on this very group.  Thank y'all muchly for them.

This fortune cookie contains spoilers and gloating!  Read it?

You feel both spoiled and patronised.

My samurai (sorry, just called him by my name; boring, I know) began
life quite innocuously.  I really don't remember a lot of detail of his
early life, except that it was new moon ("Be careful tonight!" -- so I was).

I deliberately proceeded slowly, eating everything non-poisonous and
avoiding the Mines; I would not go down stairs until I'd gained a level.
Fortunately, levels 2 and 3 had big general stores (food for the careful
shopper) and Level 3 an altar, which happened to be lawful.  (This is
*bad* luck?)  On level 2, there was a suspicious-looking gray stone, but
it wouldn't move when I kicked it, so I left it alone.  The first goblin I
killed was wearing an orcish cap +4, so there was more luck there.

I was about level 5 when I decided to try the Mines.  By this time, I'd
eaten a leprechaun (that always adds a bit of spice to the game) and emptied
a vault.  Just for the gold, you understand.

Those Mines are great for making levels quickly!  On the second level of
the Mines, there was a lamp.  What the hell... rubbed it, and got lucky;
the Genie granted me a wish!  +2 GDSM, thank you.

Wandered about the shops; bought seven candles and a very expensive bag (BoH).
Safe to buy stuff, even when you're teleporting; just drop the gold to get
some credit up.

Cleaned out the mines, got the treasure hidden in the bottom.  Was getting
quite frustrated, as my strength had dropped from 18/02 to 6 trying to
get poison resistance.  FINALLY, bottom level of the mines, got it.  Two
steps later, a potion of Restore Ability was just lying there.  Very lucky.
Wandered out, about xp level 10.

It was fairly basic hack-and-slash, right down to the Big level.  Things got
a bit hairy here; luckily one of the idiot hill orcs had found a wand of
digging and dug an escape route right next to the stairs up.

There was a ghost on level 20; a Barbarian who'd ventured too near the
swamp and met an eel.  He had some useful gear, including a ring of
conflict and some boots which turned out to be water-walking.  (Discovered
by accident -- the closest I came to premature death.  "How the h*ll did
I... oh my GOD!  Those boots...").

I found another wish about level 16 or so; GoP.  Very lucky; found only
one scroll of genocide, and it was blessed.  No more Ls.

I still wasn't experienced enough for the Quest by the time I'd found the
Medusa level, and, worse, I had no water-walking or levitation boots/rings!
All I had was holy water and one potion of levitation.  And, of course, a
pickaxe, telepathy, blindfold, looking glass, and other assorted stuff no
adventurer would be without.  Oh -- no musical instrument either.

By this time, I was invisible (blessed potion), seeing invisible (stalker
corpse), teleporting and telepathic.

So I dug through the floor (pickaxe), blessed the levitation, quaffed it
(300 moves, thank you, Gerald), and ran around the back of the castle.
Opened the backdoor, floated over the trapdoors, opened the throne room,
and watched the critters beat each other to death.  When I eventually
tracked down the WoW, I wished for a ring of levitation (couldn't
remember whether they were "boots of levitation" or "levitation boots").

Back to the Medusa level, killed M with the ol' blindfold/looking glass
trick, back down and through the castle.  Oooh -- some yummy wraiths,
which knocked me high enough to start the Quest.

Have you any idea how easy the Samurai Quest is if you've got Conflict,
Invisibility and Telepathy?  The Big Bad Dude at the end was beating up
his cronies more than myself (just as well, too; I still hadn't got the
hang of weight management, and was Stressed).  I killed him.

GoP + ToM = kick ass.  The rest of the game was fairly straightforward,
even though I only had half an idea what I was doing (thanks to some
spoilers from this group.  How do I leave the Quest?  Do I really need
to check the entire bottom level for the Vibrating Square? etc.)

Prayed for some Holy Water level 15 after dealing with Vlad.  Hmm,
I'm Hand of Elbereth now.  Wonder what *that* means?

Picked up every scroll and potion I could; cancelled all the nasty ones;
#dipped the waters into a holy water; blessed the blank scrolls; blessed
my 3 magic markers, and got down to some serious writing.  Rustproofed
all armour (I'd been making do with grease up till now), pushed it all
up to +3 or 4, identified all my amulets and gems, and still had about
20 scrolls left over.  Dropped them all in the Valley of the Dead, and
pushed on, with my AC now at -20.  (Those priests just kept taking my
gold, and didn't give me a darn thing in return!  What's with that?)

I engraved the Amulet "the Real Thing (tm)".  Good thing, too.

The Wizard got close to killing me once.  He'd Double Troubled on me,
and stolen the AoY, the BoO, CoI, BoD; and then he got me angry by
stealing the ToM (+5 by now).  GRRRR!  I teleported away (I'd recharged
the castle WoW with a scroll; second wish = Ring of teleport control)
to the stairs down, wrested a third wish from the WoW = cockatrice corpse,
and made a Wizard statue.  His double made no appearance (he'd gone upstairs,
but I didn't know), so I chipped the statue open -- there were all the
artifacts, except for AoY (it was an imitation).  Mad panic ensued as I raced
about, looking for the other WoY, who obviously had the Amulet.  Eventually,
dispirited, I gave up and went up the stairs; and there he was.  I sliced
him in half and recovered my prize.  I'd bottomed out at 55 hit points (of
about 200).

Mostly, the game was boring.  RAN upstairs (there's a monster in my way?
He dies; everything else can live).  Lots of maze levels, and those Elemental
levels are a real drag.  (Check *EVERY* square?  You're joking, surely?)
The Astral level was total chaos, with Angels of all types having at me,
High Priests, named characters I've never heard of; I just wandered,
happened into the centre of the screen, where I was greeted with the
friendly temple message, and quickly #offered what I had.

Ascension.  I was level 20, with 208 hit points; all told, I'd killed
over 2000 monsters (the WoY 10 times) and made it with about 4.5 million
points.

Now, I try again, with a tourist.

